# =============================================================================
# PopolaLoom .gitignore
#
# Intentionally NEVER ignored (DevolaFlow tracked surfaces, see bottom note):
#   .local/**, .rules/**, AGENTS.md, .cursor/rules/**
# =============================================================================


# === OS / IDE ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/


# === Cursor IDE (per-user state) ===
# Ignore everything under .cursor/ (logs, scratch, per-user agent state, etc.),
# BUT keep the compiled DevolaFlow rules under .cursor/rules/ tracked. The
# leading-slash-free pattern matches the .cursor folder at any depth, and the
# negation re-includes the rules subdir so the compile step (devola-init local)
# can publish .cursor/rules/repo-governance.mdc into version control.
.cursor/*
!.cursor/rules/


# === Python ===
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
build/
dist/
wheels/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/


# === Node / JS ===
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/
.yarn/


# === Env / Secrets ===
# Ignore .env files (which typically hold API keys / DB URLs / secrets) but
# always keep .env.example checked in as the canonical schema reference.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example


# === Logs / Temp / Scratch ===
*.log
*.tmp
tmp/
temp/
*.bak


# =============================================================================
# DO NOT IGNORE — DevolaFlow tracked surfaces
# =============================================================================
# The following paths are produced and consumed by the DevolaFlow toolchain
# (devola-init local + the .rules/ governance compiler) and MUST remain
# tracked in git so the workflow is reproducible across clones / CI:
#
#   .local/                              — local agent workspace (handoffs,
#                                          memory, feedbacks, tasks, specs)
#   .rules/                              — governance source layers
#   .rules/compile-config.yaml           — compiler config (template seed)
#   .rules/.compile-hashes.json          — drift-detection hashes (auto-gen)
#   AGENTS.md                            — compiled corpus for Codex / generic
#   .cursor/rules/repo-governance.mdc    — compiled corpus for Cursor IDE
#
# None of the rules above match these paths. If a future rule starts shadowing
# them, add an explicit `!path/here` negation in the appropriate section.
# =============================================================================
